  "result": "I searched the archive and read the closest candidates. I found no ticket that matches this problem, so I'm finalising the answer now.\n\n```json\n{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no earlier ticket that reports this exact crash. The archive has many 0xc000027b (STATUS_STOWED_EXCEPTION) fail-fasts in Windows.UI.Xaml.dll, but they have different triggers: tab drag (terminal#15689, terminal#16326), clicking in the padding area (terminal#19667), startup, and clipboard copy. None involves ListViewBase::OnKeyDown, a GettingFocus re-entrancy, or a fullscreen game running. The two tickets you cited as possibly related (#20512 and #18040) are not in the archive, so I couldn't check them. Please file this as a new issue and include the symbolised stack. Offer the full crash dumps, because the inner exception can't be read from the minidump. Say that the crashes only happen while a fullscreen exclusive game runs on another display, and that focus crosses a DPI boundary (100% to 300%). Until it is fixed, you could avoid switching focus to Terminal while the game is fullscreen. Running the game in borderless-windowed mode may also help, but nothing in the archive confirms that.\"}\n```",
